Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 12:09:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: skip redundant fn=0 phantom-vendor re-read in
 pci_scan_slot
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="------------false"

This is a multi-part message in MIME format.
--------------false
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8; format=fixed
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

---
 drivers/pci/probe.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)


--------------false
Content-Type: text/x-patch; name="0157-PCI-skip-redundant-fn-0-phantom-vendor-re-read-in-pc.patch"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="0157-PCI-skip-redundant-fn-0-phantom-vendor-re-read-in-pc.patch"

diff --git a/drivers/pci/probe.c b/drivers/pci/probe.c
index 6ca0a1ea3ad183f364f038e427dc8e0cdadf79c6..a89e2e07458b11e66aad918b2ebffb4bd76a0190 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/probe.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/probe.c
@@ -2889,7 +2889,8 @@ int pci_scan_slot(struct pci_bus *bus, int devfn)
 	}
 
 	do {
-		if (PCI_SLOT(devfn) != AEOLIA_SLOT_NUM &&
+		/* fn == 0 was already checked above; avoid re-reading it */
+		if (fn > 0 && PCI_SLOT(devfn) != AEOLIA_SLOT_NUM &&
 		    pci_bus_read_dev_vendor_id(bus, devfn + fn, &l, 60*1000) &&
 		    (l & 0xffff) == PCI_VENDOR_ID_SONY) {
 				fn = next_fn(bus, dev, fn);

--------------false--


